x86_64-linux  three strategy differences, none an ABI name. V's default constructor nobody wrote is emitted as a function here (_ZN1VC1Ev) where clang stores the vptr inline; `g(V())` passes a temporary by value, which cxx1 does through the implicit move constructor (_ZN1VC1EOS_, C2) and clang elides by building the argument in place; and clang guards `new V()` against a throwing constructor with a cleanup that names operator delete (_ZdlPv), which cxx1 emits none of - the same cleanup virtual-dtor.nonames records. What the case checks is the values, which agree on every line.
x86_64-windows  the same move constructor cxx1 emits for `g(V())` (??0V@@QEAA@$$QEAU0@@Z) and the same cleanup delete (??3@YAXPEAX@Z) on clang's side; every other name agrees.
arm64-darwin  the move constructor again, and clang's cleanup for `new V()` here is spelled _Unwind_Resume and __ZdlPv; every other name agrees.
